// Mission TT4_2, OpenTT's own map: generated.
// Cortex Craters (tt4_2): OpenTT's own Moon map (a 416 m mission area, gravity 0.45).
// Layout (x east, y north; green spawns south, blue north):
// the brain    the field folded like a brain cortex: winding sulci (trenches 6 m deep)
// and gyri (ridges) about 50 m apart, the longitudinal fissure (8 m) north
// and south of the mesa, a trench round the brain's edge;
// (0, 0)       the mesa (r 40 m, 13 m up) with a lunar base on top: a lander on its
// landing pad, a domed module, radar dishes and solar panels; two
// half-turn ramps spiral up from its south and north foot; the reload
// arch at its south foot, leading into the south ramp;
// (-118, 20), (-84, -134)  big craters (r 46, 38), (112, -30), (78, 136) big
// craters (r 50, 36) with a jump pad on the floor, ice in the northern one;
// a few small craters, boulder fields on the rims; boost pads across the middle,
// health east and west.
// See tt_assets::data::mission.
